{
 "id": "voting-11-voters",
 "title": {
  "zh-TW": "十一人投票：11–0 的大勝",
  "en": "Eleven voters: a landslide of 11–0"
 },
 "subtitle": {
  "zh-TW": "十一票全投給同一人，沒有任何一票是關鍵，可是每一票都算原因。",
  "en": "All eleven votes go to one candidate; no single vote is pivotal, yet each counts as a cause."
 },
 "family": "actual",
 "story": {
  "zh-TW": "考慮投票的情境。十一位投票人要選出一位當選人，過半數即當選。B 先生以十一票對零票勝出。拿掉任何一位投給他的人，他仍然當選。假如換成六票對五票，則每一位投給他的人都是關鍵：少一票，他就落選。",
  "en": "Eleven voters choose between two candidates, and a majority wins. Mr. B wins by eleven votes to none. Remove any single voter for him and he still wins. Change the scene to six votes to five, and every voter for him is pivotal: one vote fewer and he loses."
 },
