  "text": {
   "zh-TW": "每一位投給 B 先生的人都促成了他的當選。在大勝中，單獨一票的分量比險勝時輕得多。",
   "en": "Every voter for Mr. B helped him win, though in a landslide a single vote weighs much less than in a narrow win."
  },
  "agree": [
   "hp-original",
   "hp-updated"
  ]
 },
 "explanation": {
  "zh-TW": "X1 到 X11 各代表一位投票人，投給 B 先生為 1。O 表示 B 先生當選，條件是至少六票。引擎的方程式只支援布林運算，所以另設兩個計票變數：T1 計前六位、T2 計後五位，兩者合計至少六時 O 成立。這兩個變數只用來記帳，不屬於故事。實際情境是 11–0（Halpern 2016 例 2.3.2）。showcase 的第一項讓後五位改投 G 先生，呈現 6–5 的情境。",
  "en": "X1 to X11 stand for the eleven voters, with 1 meaning a vote for Mr. B; O says Mr. B wins, which takes at least six votes. The engine's equations support only Boolean operations, so there are two tally variables: T1 counts the votes of the first six voters, T2 counts those of the last five, and O holds when the two total at least six. They are bookkeeping and not part of the story. The context is 11–0: by plain counterfactual dependence no single vote is a cause. The original and updated HP definitions make a vote pivotal under the supposition that five other voters switch, so every voter is a cause; the modified HP definition allows no such change, and only a group of six voters together forms a cause, each voter being part of a cause (Halpern 2016, Ex. 2.3.2). Degree of responsibility is 1/(N+1), where N is the number of other votes that must change first: 1/6 for each voter at 11–0, and 1 for each at 6–5 (Chockler and Halpern 2004, Ex. 3.3). Responsibility is not one of the engine's theories, and the 6–5 scene is not this case's context; the first showcase item (the last five voters switch to Mr. G) shows it, with Mr. B still winning 6–5."
 },
